WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0034: BG3's figures skinned on the GPU.
A third companion broke the 82 fps lockstep: wowbg3_tav skinned every vertex of every figure on the
CPU each frame and uploaded them. Now each mesh goes up once per plan in BG3's bind pose with BG3's
weights and bones as WoW's joint attributes, holds a slot of benilla's own rig palette (the lane WoW's
units skin from), and each pose writes only the slot: the figure frame (world transform and world
mode's mapping, from the figure's root) and BG3's own bone palette (wowbg3_tav rig_rows). rig_palette
gains RigPalettes::write_rows (caller-composed rows; the slot's origin word w = 1); wow_model.wgsl
skins such a slot as BG3's SkinningCompute does: F.B.[p,1], tangent frames turned by the rotation of
the row-normalised blend (bg3_bone_rotation; the CPU path now does the same). WOW_BG3_TAV_SKIN=cpu
keeps the CPU path (A/B, rollback); =ab adds an in-game A/B (skin-ab request); WOW_BG3_TAV_SKIN_CHECK=N
checks every N-th pose against the CPU path vertex by vertex. LODs: with a layer that flags which
planned meshes BG3 drew each frame (the LOD format research), exactly those are drawn; else LOD 0.
